       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. You didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't find one. The order is 12,750 mg per day, about 5 times the maximum, and each 4,250 mg dose is in the range seen in metformin overdose. I think it could seriously harm the patient. It's also a hard stop I shouldn't bypass through order entry.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, metformin 850 mg orally three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day), or a lower starting dose with titration.\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"dose confirmed with department chair,\" if you decide on a different dose within the labeled range.\n- **Route a true off-label request through pharmacy.** If you believe a dose above the labeled maximum is necessary, it should go through pharmacist review and your institution's override process. I can't make that decision for you.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
